---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Cookie Policy" description="Cookies, local storage, analytics, advertising, and visitor controls on SecureByteGuide.">
  <article class="container mx-auto px-6 md:px-10 py-16 md:py-24 max-w-3xl">
    <header class="mb-12"><p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.25em] font-mono text-accent mb-4">SecureByteGuide · Trust</p><h1 class="text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold leading-[0.95] mb-4" style="font-family:var(--font-display);">Cookie Policy</h1><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated: September 6, 2026</p></header>
    <div class="prose-article space-y-8 text-[16px] leading-[1.75]">
<section><h2>What these technologies do</h2><p>Cookies are small browser records. Local storage is a related browser feature. SecureByteGuide may use them for essential preferences, security, aggregate analytics, or advertising when those services are active. A normal page request also creates hosting and security logs that are not browser cookies.</p></section>
<section><h2>Categories</h2><ul><li><strong>Necessary and preference storage:</strong> supports page delivery, abuse prevention, and remembered browser choices.</li><li><strong>Analytics:</strong> may measure visits and page performance in aggregate.</li><li><strong>Advertising:</strong> Google AdSense may set or read cookies when advertising is enabled, subject to applicable consent and Google policies.</li><li><strong>External services:</strong> a merchant, video host, or linked provider may use its own technologies after you open its service.</li></ul></section>
<section><h2>Your controls</h2><p>You can block, delete, or limit cookies in browser settings. You can review Google advertising choices in <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/">My Ad Center</a>. Blocking storage may prevent preferences or embedded services from working as intended. Where a consent control is presented, use it to make the choices available in your region.</p></section>
<section><h2>Contact</h2><p>For questions about this policy, email <a href="mailto:editor@securebyteguide.org">editor@securebyteguide.org</a>. See the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for broader information-handling details.</p></section></div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
